  ('Bachelor of Electrical Engineering Technology (Industrial Power) with Honours', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UTeM University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 3788, '4 years', '["Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Electrical Engineering Technology (Industrial Power) with Honours program at UTeM University Malaysia focuses on various aspects of the electricity system, including generation, transmission, power distribution, power system protection, electrical energy, load management, regulatory affairs, and energy components such as circuit breakers and transformer control equipment. It is designed to provide students with a comprehensive understanding of industrial power systems and equip them with the necessary skills and knowledge to work in the field.

Graduates Electrical engineering technology (EET) is an engineering technology field that implements and applies the principles of electrical engineering. The role of electrical engineering technologists is primarily to design, develop, test, and manufacture electrical and electronic equipment and they may work in product evaluation and testing, using measuring and diagnostic devices to adjust, test, and repair equipment. Graduates of electrical engineering technology programs capable of accommodate a wide range of career fields, such as:

Thank you  for submitting your form to us. We will contact you as soon as possible to assist you on your university journey.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Graduates Electrical engineering technology (EET) is an engineering technology field that implements and applies the principles of electrical engineering. The role of electrical engineering technologists is primarily to design, develop, test, and manufacture electrical and electronic equipment and they may work in product evaluation and testing, using measuring and diagnostic devices to adjust, test, and repair equipment. Graduates of electrical engineering technology programs capable of accommodate a wide range of career fields, such as:\n\nTelecommunications and signal processing\nMedical technology and devices\nAerospace and avionics\nTransportation\nComputers\nElectrical power industry and power distribution\nOptoelectronics\nResearch and development\nProcess Control\nManufacturing Industries"]'::jsonb, 'Fees Applies', 'Pass Matriculation / Foundation / STPM or equivalent.'),
  ('Bachelor of Electrical Engineering Technology with Honours', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UTeM University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 3788, '4 years', '["Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Electrical Engineering Technology with Honours program at UTeM University Malaysia prepares students to work in various electrical engineering disciplines. The curriculum includes a balanced mix of core and elective engineering courses, combining theoretical, practical, and soft skill elements to develop well-rounded engineers. The program is designed to align with the university''s and faculty''s missions, as well as the Program Educational Objectives (PEOs). The curriculum focuses on producing competent graduates who meet industry needs. Key components of the program include laboratory work, industrial training, integrated design projects, and final year projects. The curriculum also emphasizes engineering application, professional ethics, and exposure to engineering practice through guest lectures, industry visits, and courses on professional conduct.

Vacancies within the industries for engineers that are skilled and practical-oriented is on the rise. Lots of highly trained workforces in the entire engineering sector including Industry Power, Control, Instrumentation and Automation, Power Electronics and Drive and Mechatronics in professional level are required. Job opportunities for UTeM graduates in these fields will be more desirable by the industry once they have been equipped with the technical knowledge and strong practical skills.

Field of works for Bachelor of Electrical Engineering and Mechatronics Engineering graduates include:

Some of the career fields that are suitable include Process and Manufacturing Engineer, Design and Research Engineer, Consultancies Engineer, Testing and Quality Engineer, System Engineer and Academicians.

Thank you  for submitting your form to us. We will contact you as soon as possible to assist you on your university journey.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Vacancies within the industries for engineers that are skilled and practical-oriented is on the rise. Lots of highly trained workforces in the entire engineering sector including Industry Power, Control, Instrumentation and Automation, Power Electronics and Drive and Mechatronics in professional level are required. Job opportunities for UTeM graduates in these fields will be more desirable by the industry once they have been equipped with the technical knowledge and strong practical skills.\n\nField of works for Bachelor of Electrical Engineering and Mechatronics Engineering graduates include:\n\nSemiconductor manufacturing industries\nElectrical items manufacturing\nHigh and Low Voltage components manufacturing\nRenewable Energy sector\nOil and Gas Industries\nConsultancies Companies\nHigh technology industries such as aerospace industries\nAutomation System manufacturing industries\nBiomedical Engineering Firms\nSoftware Development Sector\nResearch and development Sector\n\nSome of the career fields that are suitable include Process and Manufacturing Engineer, Design and Research Engineer, Consultancies Engineer, Testing and Quality Engineer, System Engineer and Academicians."]'::jsonb, 'Fees Applies', 'Pass Matriculation / Foundation / STPM or equivalent.'),
