  ('Bachelor of Electronic Engineering with Honours', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UTeM University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 3788, '4 years', '["Feb","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Electronic Engineering with Honours program at UTeM University Malaysia combines engineering science, mathematics, and electrical and electronic engineering principles. It aims to develop students'' mastery of electronic engineering and problem-solving skills. The program offers specialization options in computer engineering, industrial electronics, telecommunication electronics, or wireless communication in the final year. Students gain a solid theoretical foundation and develop generic skills for research, presentation, and implementation of engineering solutions.

Graduates in electronic engineering have excellent career prospects. They can work as industrial electronic engineers, computer engineers, telecommunication engineers, and wireless communication engineers. They can also pursue academic careers as lecturers and researchers. Graduates can practice as professional engineers locally and internationally. Entrepreneurship is another option for self-employment and success in their areas of expertise.

