  ('Bachelor of Information Technology (Games Technology) with Honours', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UTeM University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 3155, '4 years', '["Feb","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Information Technology (Games Technology) with Honours program at UTeM University Malaysia prepares graduates with specialized knowledge and skills in computer games technology. They gain expertise in areas such as game programming, game design, 2D and 3D game development, and project management. Graduates can pursue careers in game-based education, game content development, and roles such as game programmers, game designers, game developers, and game project managers.

A wide range of career opportunities in the field of computer science and information technology is open to graduates who specialized in computer games. Among the career opportunities such as game designer, game developer, game programmer, game animator, game audio engineer, game tester, technical support, and specialist computer game researcher.

