  ('Bachelor of Manufacturing Engineering Technology (Process and Technology) with Honours', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UTeM University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 3788, '4 years', '["Feb","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The objectives of the Bachelor of Manufacturing Engineering Technology (Process and Technology) with Honours program at UTeM University Malaysia are to equip graduates with knowledge in Manufacturing Engineering Technology, adaptability to evolving technologies, and professional ethics and leadership skills. Graduates will be able to apply engineering principles, solve problems, collaborate in teams, communicate effectively, and engage in lifelong learning.

The Bachelor of Manufacturing Engineering Technology (Process & Technology) program teaches students the practical and theoretical aspects of manufacturing processes for different materials and products. From basic fabrication to advanced CNC machining, students gain hands-on experience and knowledge in various processes. The program emphasizes design, operation, control, and optimization for the transfer of research and technology into practical and cost-effective processes.

*** For General Elective, students may choose any ONE (1) subject from the list below:

