  ('DOCTOR OF TECHNOLOGY MANAGEMENT', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UTeM University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'PhD', 4535, '3 years', '["Feb","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Doctor of Technology Management (DTM) program at UTeM University, Malaysia, is a three-year program that consists of 1.5 years of coursework followed by 1.5 years of research study. Candidates are required to complete 48 credits of coursework and 32 credits for research.

This program emphasizes contemporary management thinking, focusing on real-world, business-oriented critical thinking and problem-solving skills integrated into both coursework and research activities. The DTM degree provides a theoretical foundation applicable to managing high-tech organizations, equipping candidates with the relevant knowledge and skills to advance their careers.

The program employs a variety of learning methods, including blended learning, case study analysis, problem-based assignments, industrial talks, and presentations. The experience gained during the coursework enriches candidates'' knowledge and prepares them for their research journey.

During the research phase, candidates are supervised by faculty academic staff and must undergo a viva-voce session in the final semester. The degree is awarded upon completion of coursework, successful completion of the oral examination, and submission of the research thesis.

Candidates interested in joining this program may submit their applications throughout the year, with studies beginning in common semesters according to the university''s academic calendar. Successful candidates will earn the title of Doctor of Technology Management (DTM) upon fulfilling all requirements.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Specialist in field"]'::jsonb, 'Fees Applies', 'A relevant master degree with at least CGPA 2.75 in related field from any accredited institutions of higher learning recognised and approved by the Senate

