  ('Bachelor (Hons) in Finance', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Sunway University' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 7088, '3 years', '["Feb","Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor (Honours) in Finance program is designed to cultivate versatile graduates in Banking and Finance by providing a solid foundation in a diverse array of subjects, including Accounting, Banking, Fintech, Investment, and Quantitative Methods, to meet the demands of today’s industry. The curriculum includes specialized training and skill development in key national priority areas, along with an intensive two-semester applied project and an internship with securities firms. Students will also be well-prepared to pursue higher-level professional qualifications such as the Chartered Financial Analyst (CFA) and the Chartered Banker (CB) certification offered by the Asian Institute of Chartered Bankers.

Graduates of the Bachelor in Finance will be equipped to launch successful careers across a wide range of organizations, from small businesses (as all firms require financial expertise) to traditional banks, financial institutions, and innovative Silicon Valley-style startups, including Digital Asset Exchanges. They will also be prepared to embrace the challenges of the Fourth Industrial Revolution.

