  ('Bachelor of Arts (Honors) Global Management', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Sunway University' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 4804, '4 years', '["Feb","Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Arts (Honors) in Global Management at Sunway University is a forward-thinking degree designed to equip students with the essential skills, knowledge, and mindset needed to thrive in an increasingly interconnected and dynamic global business environment. This interdisciplinary program combines core business principles with global strategy, emerging technologies, cross-cultural communication, and leadership development.

The curriculum balances theoretical foundations with practical application, allowing students to navigate the complexities of managing across borders, collaborating with diverse teams, and responding to global economic trends. Emphasis is placed on strategic thinking, data literacy, ethical decision-making, and the ability to lead in multicultural and digitally-driven settings. Additionally, students will enhance their communication, analytical, and problem-solving skills—key attributes for success in any global career. This program is based on the esteemed Bachelor of Global Management at the Thunderbird School of Global Management, Arizona State University, USA, further ensuring its relevance and rigor in today''s global marketplace.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

