  ('Bachelor of Arts (Honours) in Interior Architecture', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Sunway University' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 6633, '3.5 years', '["Feb","Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Arts (Honours) in Interior Architecture is an engaging program tailored for students aspiring to become innovative interior architecture professionals in the 21st century. Over a span of 3.5 years, you will explore various aspects of design for interior environments, developing the skills needed to contribute to the profession with creativity and confidence.

The curriculum is delivered across diverse learning environments, starting with studio experiences that immerse you in the fundamentals of the design process and thinking. This approach fosters knowledge and skill development in creating interactions between people and interior spaces. You will study a well-rounded blend of theoretical and practical subjects, including design practice, modeling, drawing, furniture design, and sustainable design. A strong sense of design, combined with effective communication skills and proficiency in the latest technology, will prepare you for a career in any design field.

