  ('Bachelor of Arts (Honours) in Theatre Production', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Sunway University' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 7729, '3 years', '["Jan","Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Arts (Honours) in Theatre Production is a comprehensive program that explores the dynamic practices of contemporary theatre-making. Students will refine their skills in performance, directing, design, and production management, supported by critical studies of history, context, and theory.

The curriculum also addresses the production of theatre in an increasingly digital landscape. Graduates will emerge with foundational skills in leadership, innovation, self-sustainability, and arts entrepreneurship.

This innovative program is taught by theatre practitioners and academics with diverse experiences, perspectives, and methodologies. In addition to lectures and practical studio sessions, students engage in tutorials, individual and group projects, guided research, fieldwork, and field trips.

