  ('Master in Medical Science', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Sunway University' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 4719, '2 years', '["Apr"]'::jsonb, 'The Master in Medical Science is a research-focused program designed for graduates with a bachelor''s degree in medical science or a related discipline who wish to enhance their research skills in this field. The program aims to foster a comprehensive understanding and offers opportunities for national and international collaborations, specialized training activities (such as seminars and workshops), and extensive clinical research experience.

Medical science explores the biological mechanisms that govern the human body''s functions, emphasizing the diagnosis, treatment, and prevention of diseases. The scope of research in medical science is extensive, encompassing areas from basic biology to oncology, chemistry to pharmacology, and physics to radiotherapy.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

This is a taught course and students are required to pass this module before the commencement of project. Students will have a designated supervisor who is a member of academic staff with research expertise in the student’s area of study.

At the end of work completion, students are expected to submit their Master’s thesis for examination and attend a defence for their thesis.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Lecturer/Medical Educator\nResearcher\nClinical Research Coordinator\nScientific/Medical Writer"]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'Bachelor’s degree in Medical Sciences with minimum CGPA of 2.75 or equivalent, as accepted by the Sunway University Senate.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.'),
  ('Master in Public Policy', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Sunway University' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 10437, '1 year', '["Jan","May","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master in Public Policy offered by the Jeffrey Cheah Institute on Southeast Asia equips students to create effective solutions for real-world policy challenges in the region. The program adopts a multidisciplinary approach, emphasizing economics, quantitative analysis, and public policy management.

Designed for both graduates and mid-career professionals, this program enhances technical skills in evidence-based policy analysis. It also deepens understanding of essential concepts and current issues related to economic development, social inclusion, political governance, and technological advancements.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

This programme is a 1-2 year programme of 8 modules including 4 core modules, 2 capstone research projects and 2 electives.

