  ('Master in Sustainable Development Management', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Sunway University' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 12012, '1 year', '["Mar"]'::jsonb, 'The Master in Sustainable Development Management (MSDM) at the Jeffrey Sachs Center is designed to cultivate a new generation of multidisciplinary practitioners skilled in management and problem-solving through analytics and systems thinking, with a focus on global challenges. This program aims to equip students with essential management abilities to devise innovative solutions that align with the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).

The curriculum covers various topics, including corporate sustainability strategies, social entrepreneurship, finance and sustainability, sustainable management and operations, and economics and development. It draws on a comprehensive knowledge base that addresses critical areas such as climate change, waste management, energy systems, agriculture and food systems, forestry, and biodiversity.

Students will engage with both theoretical frameworks and practical applications, including real-world case studies, to develop a well-rounded understanding of the opportunities and challenges involved in achieving the SDGs across scientific, economic, business, and technological domains.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

Students are required to complete 10 core courses, including Research Projects I & II, and 4 elective courses.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Innovators\nSocial entrepreneurs\nEducators\nConsultants\nPolitical leaders\nCivil society activists"]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'A bachelor’s degree (Level 6, MQF) or its equivalent, with a minimum CGPA of 2.50 out of 4.00

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.'),
  ('Master of Applied Behaviour Analysis', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Sunway University' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 7986, '2 years', '["Apr"]'::jsonb, 'This programme is designed to prepare graduates to become Malaysia Certified Behaviour Analysts by fulfilling the required supervised practice hours in accordance with the training guidelines set by the Malaysia Association of Behaviour Analysis. Sunway University proudly stands as the first and only institution in Southeast Asia offering the Master of Applied Behaviour Analysis programme.

The curriculum encompasses a variety of theoretical and practical elements of applied behaviour analysis. Graduates will gain skills in analyzing and modifying behaviour through the application of these principles across various industries and situations that necessitate behavioural change or maintenance. They will develop a deep understanding of these concepts and learn to apply them effectively in diverse contexts, enabling them to tackle behavioural challenges and foster positive behaviour change.

Moreover, graduates will play a key role in conducting behavioural assessments and interventions for individuals with developmental disabilities, including autism. Their responsibilities may involve designing and implementing behaviour intervention plans, performing assessments to identify specific behavioural issues, and collaborating with other professionals to provide comprehensive support.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

Students are required to complete 6 core coursework modules, 2 Research Projects, and 2 Practicum courses.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["ABA Therapist\nAcademician / Lecturer\nBehaviour Analyst\nCase Supervisor\nClinical Director\nEarly Intervention Programme Manager / Coordinator"]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'A Bachelor’s degree in Psychology or its equivalent with a minimum CGPA of 2.75 out of 4.00

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.'),
  ('Master of Arts in Creative Arts and Media', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Sunway University' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 4246, '2 years', '["Feb","Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Arts in Creative Arts and Media allows students to engage in interdisciplinary research, contributing fresh insights and understanding to fields associated with the School of Arts.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

The programme is research-based culminating in a thesis (which may include a practical creative arts component, where applicable) that demonstrates mastery of the advanced points, craft and discipline of the area of research.

The student is required to complete one taught module – Research Methods – before proceeding to the Proposal Defence. This core module introduces students to the fundamentals of academic research and methodologies at the postgraduate level to conduct an independent research project.

This is an intensive course. Classes are spread over eight weeks (12 to 15 hours per week) for Full-time or Part-time students. These classes are followed by tutorials when the students conduct their research projects. Weekly schedules may vary from one year to another.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Creative Industries\nAcademia\nArts and Culture"]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'A Bachelor''s degree in the relevant field with minimum CGPA of 2.75

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.'),
  ('Master of Arts in Visual Communication and Media Studies', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Sunway University' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 9768, '1 year', '["Feb","Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'Communications and Media are constantly evolving and play an increasingly significant role in our daily lives. Whether it''s through platforms like Netflix, Facebook, and Instagram, your favorite online game, or an interactive installation you experienced at a museum, media messaging is pervasive. Today, these messages are crafted around narratives, with branding narratives shaping the way we perceive information across all media forms. In this program, we will explore these concepts through the lens of narratives, examining how contemporary media has developed storytelling as an organizing principle and its implications for society.

You will learn how messages are constructed and their impact on our culture and society. This program will enable you to analyze how different media shape the transmission and definition of messages and how emerging technologies influence the content we receive. You will acquire this knowledge through a blend of theoretical frameworks and practical experiences. Additionally, you will develop a research-based thesis project that merges creative and academic research methodologies. This approach fosters knowledge and innovation through artistic expression, scholarly inquiry, and experimentation, culminating in an original artistic work accompanied by a scholarly component.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

This programme is an MA by coursework. You will take six (6) core courses in research, media theory and media practise. From there you will chose two (2) electives in either theory, practise or both. The MA culminates in a Research-Creation Project as a final work. This project will utilise research methodologies in order to create unique visual works expressing the knowledge gained form your research.

Thank you  for submitting your form to us. We will contact you as soon as possible to assist you on your university journey.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Identity Branding\nCorporate Communications\nCommunication Design\nNew Media Design"]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'A Bachelor’s degree or its equivalent, with a minimum CGPA of 2.75

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.'),
  ('Master of Business Administration', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Sunway University' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 4950, '2 years', '["Jan","Mar","May","Jul","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Online Master of Business Administration at Sunway University aims to strike a balance between essential business knowledge and future leadership skills.

