  ('Master of Science in Actuarial Analytics', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Sunway University' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 9790, '1 year', '["Feb","May","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Science in Actuarial Analytics at Sunway University, accredited by the Institute and Faculty of Actuaries (IFoA), offers a streamlined pathway for graduates. Upon completion, students are eligible for exemptions from the CP1, CP2, and CP3 papers, facilitating a fast track toward qualifying as an Associate of the IFoA. The program equips students with essential analytical skills and exposure to AI-related techniques, ensuring their relevance and practical application in the workplace.

Designed specifically for actuarial students seeking professional qualification, this program provides three additional CP exemptions from the IFoA, enabling a seamless transition from undergraduate studies and accelerating their journey toward becoming qualified actuaries. This comprehensive approach not only prepares students for the actuarial profession but also empowers them to deliver valuable contributions to their organizations.

Bachelor’s degree in Actuarial Science or related fields with a CGPA ≥ 2.50, as accepted by the Academic Senate.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g.,Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

Thank you  for submitting your form to us. We will contact you as soon as possible to assist you on your university journey.', '[{"year":"Year 1","modules":["Actuarial Practice 1","Actuarial Practice 2","Actuarial Modelling","Professional Communication","Machine Learning","Predictive Models and Clustering Algorithm","Research Methodology","Research Project 1","Research Project 2"]}]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Actuary\nActuarial Reserving Analyst\nCatastrophe Risk Analyst\nData Scientist\nData Engineer\nAnalyst (Financial, Investment Data, Risk, Business, etc.)\nRegulator\nMachine Learning Scientist\nInvestment and Portfolio Manager\nRisk Manager\nAcademia\nStatistician\nMathematician"]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'Bachelor’s degree in Actuarial Science or related fields with a CGPA ≥ 2.50, as accepted by the Academic Senate.

