  ('Master of Science in Applied Mathematics', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Sunway University' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 10120, '1 year', '["Jan","Mar","May","Jul","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'Mathematics serves as a vital language for invention, innovation, and the generation of ideas. Applied mathematicians are essential in various ongoing initiatives by individuals, organizations, businesses, and governments to address issues impacting the livelihoods of large segments of humanity, mitigate potential future threats to planetary health, and safeguard our planet to ensure the survival of our species.

Sunway University’s MSc in Applied Mathematics program prepares graduates with an innovative mindset, enabling them to apply mathematical tools and knowledge to develop practical solutions for a wide range of challenges in the physical and medical sciences, engineering, technology, finance, investment, business, commerce, and social sciences.

The School of Mathematical Sciences (SMS) features experienced professors, associate professors, and senior lecturers who teach all modules, supported by a dedicated team to assist students in their studies. Among the faculty is a professor recognized as a World Top 2% Scientist, who has a robust network of researchers globally, particularly in ASEAN and China. This professor has an outstanding track record in optimization and optimal control, leading the team in module delivery. Consequently, graduates of the MSc in Applied Mathematics gain a competitive edge over those from similar programs at other universities. SMS also offers various activities, including seminars, research talks, and training sessions, to equip students with soft skills and the latest information.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

