  ('MSc in Life Sciences', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Sunway University' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 4246, '2 years', '["Jan","Jul"]'::jsonb, 'This postgraduate research program offers students the opportunity to conduct original research that expands knowledge in a specialized area of their choice within the Life Sciences.

The program provides advanced training in research methods, enabling students to apply their knowledge and skills as researchers, practitioners, and administrators across various fields of life sciences. This training will also assist them in securing employment in the healthcare and biopharmaceutical industries.

The MSc in Life Sciences is offered in collaboration with Lancaster University, UK. Upon successful completion of the program, graduates will receive two certificates, recognizing them as graduates of both Sunway University and Lancaster University.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

Students will learn about current approaches to research design, data analysis and scientific writing. At the end of this module, candidates will be expected to formulate and submit a proposal for research in an area of their interest or specialisation. Candidates will also develop the necessary skills and knowledge to conduct research  successfully.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Biochemist\nEntrepreneur\nHealthcare manager\nImmunologist\nLaboratory manager\nLecturer/Science educator\nMicrobiologist"]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'A Bachelor’s Degree in Biological Sciences (e.g. Medical Biotech, Biomedicine, etc) or a related field; with minimum CGPA of 2.75 or equivalent.

