  ('MSc in Psychology', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Sunway University' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 4246, '2 years', '["Jan","Jul"]'::jsonb, 'This program centers on a topic of the student’s choice through an independent research project. It is specifically designed to help students develop research skills and conduct independent research while deepening their knowledge and understanding in an area of psychology that inspires them.

Students will learn how to review the literature and plan and manage a research project. The skills and competencies they acquire in critical thinking, project management, and report writing will enhance their career prospects. Core modules in the program ensure that students are well-versed in research methodologies and statistical techniques, enabling them to conduct effective research in various areas of psychology. These modules also aim to enhance students'' understanding of ethical issues and their ability to address research questions related to psychology.

Additionally, the program serves as an excellent foundation for students who wish to pursue further studies at the PhD level.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

The Psychology Department has three research groups: Well-being & Community Psychology, Organisational & Work Psychology, and Cognitive & Experimental Psychology. This broad range of expertise means we have research supervision in the following areas:', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Mental Health Consultant\nPsychology Lecturer\nResearch assistant"]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'A Bachelor’s degree in Psychology or equivalent with a minimum CGPA of 3.00

