  ('PhD in Medical Science', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Sunway University' LIMIT 1), 'PhD', 6508, '3 years', '["Jan","Jul"]'::jsonb, 'The Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in Medical Science is a research-focused program that engages students in bidirectional translational medicine. This program centers on studies that either bring current patient and medical care issues into laboratory settings or translate scientific discoveries made in labs or clinics into new treatments and approaches aimed at improving health and medical care in the community.

With the guidance of supervisors, students will identify a research question or topic within the realm of medical science and conduct their research independently. They are required to complete a taught module, Clinical Research Methodology, which prepares them for effective project planning and management while fostering ethical awareness and social responsibility. To graduate, students must produce a thesis based on their original research and successfully complete the thesis examination and viva voce.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g.,,Other qualifications equivalent to a Master’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

An advanced study the management of a research project. The first part discusses the design of a scientific project in health and medical settings, including research questions, hypothesis, method selection, problem solving, and data collection and analysis. The second part consists of ethical theory and ethical issues related to clinical research especially the application of ethics for utilizing human specimens. The third part of this subject focuses on the statistical analysis and its methods.

Production of thesis is based on students’ original research throughout the PhD candidature. Students must submit a PhD thesis and obtain a pass grade in the thesis examination in order to be awarded a PhD degree.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Lecturer/Medical Educator\nUniversity Professor\nResearcher\nClinical Research Coordinator\nMedical Science Consultant"]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'A Master’s degree in medical science or related fields accepted by the University Senate.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g.,,Other qualifications equivalent to a Master’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.'),
  ('PhD in Sustainable Development', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Sunway University' LIMIT 1), 'PhD', 3652, '3 years', '["Jan","Jul"]'::jsonb, 'The PhD in Sustainable Development is a comprehensive research program that focuses on critical areas of sustainable development as outlined in the 17 Sustainable Development Goals. Research topics will encompass a broad spectrum of complex issues and theories related to sustainable development, including the science of climate change and ecosystems, sustainable economics, social progress, management, public policy, environmental practices, and governance.

Students have the flexibility to choose any of the key dimensions of sustainable development and engage in in-depth research to develop insights, theories, and practical solutions that contribute to advancing the sustainability agenda.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g.,,Other qualifications equivalent to a Master’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

For this PhD programme by Research, students are required to complete a Research Methods course.  This module introduces students to the academic research and methodologies at the postgraduate level in order to conduct an independent research study.

Students must complete an in-depth research on a topic related to sustainable development in the form of a thesis. The student will be required to complete a number of academic milestones including a proposal defense and a viva voce.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Academia\nGovernment"]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'A Master’s Degree in a related field as accepted by the University Senate.

