  ('Master of Science in Finance', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'University of Southampton Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 13038, '1 year', '["Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Science in Finance program at the University of Southampton Malaysia provides students with a comprehensive understanding of finance and equips them with the essential skills required in today''s highly competitive environment. This program offers a deep exploration of finance principles, theories, and practices, enabling students to develop a specialized role or engage in research across various sectors. Whether it is the public sector, banks and financial institutions, business sectors, or universities and research-related institutions, graduates of this program are prepared to excel. The curriculum encompasses a wide range of finance topics, including financial analysis, investment management, risk assessment, financial markets, and corporate finance. Through a combination of theoretical knowledge, practical applications, and research opportunities, students gain the expertise to make informed financial decisions and address complex financial challenges. Graduates of the Master of Science in Finance program at the University of Southampton Malaysia possess the knowledge and skills to pursue diverse career opportunities. They are well-equipped to assume roles in finance departments of public and private organizations, financial institutions, consulting firms, or pursue further academic research in finance-related fields. With their specialized knowledge and analytical abilities, graduates can contribute to the growth and success of financial institutions and make a significant impact in the field of finance.

