  ('Bachelor of Commerce', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Curtin University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 8316, '3 years', '["Feb","Jul"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Commerce (Management and Marketing) program at Curtin University Malaysia offers a comprehensive education in both management and marketing, providing students with valuable knowledge and skills applicable to a wide range of industries and sectors, locally and globally. In the Management stream, students learn essential skills for leading and supervising teams, managing budgets, and successfully completing tasks and projects. They also gain an understanding of important considerations such as values, ethics, and sustainability. A management qualification opens doors to various career opportunities, and graduates may receive recognition from professional bodies. In the Marketing stream, students delve into the crucial role of marketing in business success. They learn how to differentiate products and services, effectively communicate with target audiences, and develop strategies to maximize consumer value, sales, and profits. The curriculum covers advertising, promotions, digital and social media marketing, public relations, retailing, and sales strategies to promote brands, products, and services. The program emphasizes industry interaction, with strong connections and real-life client projects where students develop strategies to solve business problems and present their ideas to management representatives.

