  ('Bachelor of Engineering (Chemical Engineering)-Honours', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Curtin University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 11132, '4 years', '["Feb","Jul"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Engineering (Chemical Engineering) (Honours) program at Curtin University Malaysia focuses on the development, design, and operation of chemical processes and plants. This field encompasses the extraction, conversion, and recovery of materials using both chemical and biological systems. Chemical engineers play a crucial role in various process industries that cater to societal needs. These industries include petroleum refining, gas processing, petrochemical and polymer production, bio-processing and bio-production, bio-pharmaceutics and food processing, fertilizer manufacture, cement and lime production, minerals and metals extraction and refining, paper and board manufacture, biomass and sugar refining, as well as the production of industrial and fine chemicals. The program equips students with the knowledge and skills necessary to contribute to these diverse sectors.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

