  ('Bachelor of Engineering (Electrical and Electronic Engineering)-Honours', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Curtin University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 11132, '4 years', '["Feb","Jul"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Engineering (Electrical and Electronic Engineering) (Honours) program at Curtin University Malaysia encompasses the fundamental technologies that underpin our everyday lives, from large-scale devices like electric vehicles to small devices like mobile phones and computers. This field covers a wide range of areas, including electrical power and control, electronic systems, telecommunication, and computer systems. Electricity plays a vital role in various aspects of modern civilization, including heating, cooling, transportation, lighting, manufacturing, and production. The study of electrical and electronic engineering involves the application of electrical energy, including its generation, transmission, distribution, as well as the utilization of renewable and sustainable energy sources. The field of electronics is rapidly expanding and is essential to industries such as robotics and telecommunications. With the advancement of the information society, such as the Internet of Things (IoT), electrical and electronic engineers play a crucial role in shaping a better future.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

