  ('Bachelor of Engineering (Energy Engineering) - Honours', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Curtin University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 11132, '4 years', '["Feb","Jul"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Engineering (Energy Engineering) (Honours) program at Curtin University Malaysia focuses on the emerging field of Energy in Transition, emphasizing energy efficiency and reducing reliance on fossil fuels. This major explores geo-energy opportunities such as geothermal and hydrogen systems, sustainable energy, environmental compliance, and conventional and emerging renewable energy technologies. The program aims to establish Curtin as a global leader in Energy and Resource Transition, aligned with international goals and regional strategies. Graduates will be well-prepared to contribute to the global advancement of Energy in Transition technologies, starting with a strong foundation in engineering concepts through the Engineering Foundation Year (EFY).

