  ('Master of Philosophy', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Curtin University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 9218, '1 year', '["Feb","Jul"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Philosophy program at Curtin University Malaysia is designed to provide an opportunity for students to expand their knowledge beyond the undergraduate honours or postgraduate diploma level, ultimately leading to the completion of a research thesis. Upon successfully completing a master''s degree by research, students have the option to apply for entry into a Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) program. A higher degree by research distinguishes itself from other postgraduate degrees by emphasizing research, which should constitute at least two-thirds of the study program. While some coursework units may be included, the core of the program involves conducting research and producing a thesis under the guidance of a supervisor and associate supervisor(s). The thesis must demonstrate, according to the examiners'' assessment, a significant and original contribution to knowledge or understanding in any field through the discovery of new facts, formulation of theories, or innovative reinterpretation of existing data and established ideas. Additionally, it should showcase the student''s ability to conceive, design, and independently execute research.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

Curtin University stands out as a leading institution for research due to its strong commitment to applied research aimed at addressing real-world challenges. The university''s research efforts are supported by robust partnerships with industry, business, and government entities, resulting in tangible outcomes that have a positive impact on the wider community at local, national, and global levels. Curtin''s reputation as a reliable collaborator in industry-driven research further enhances the opportunities available to graduates, empowering them to become trailblazers and innovators in their respective fields.

