  ('Bachelor of Engineering (Honours)', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Swinburne University of Technology Sarawak Campus' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 10595, '4 years', '["Feb","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) (Civil) program at Swinburne University of Technology Sarawak Campus focuses on the field of civil engineering, which encompasses the design, construction, and enhancement of our built environment. This degree equips students with the technical expertise and management skills necessary to plan, design, construct, and maintain various types of infrastructure. These include buildings, bridges, dams, water supply systems, waste treatment systems, roads and railways, and air and sea ports. Throughout the program, students gain a comprehensive understanding of civil engineering theory alongside practical experience through hands-on work and real-life projects. This combination ensures that students are job-ready, equipped with the necessary skills and knowledge to excel in the industry. Additionally, the program serves as a pathway for those interested in research or further learning in the field of civil engineering. By completing the Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) (Civil), students acquire a strong foundation that enables them to contribute to the development and improvement of the built environment, fostering sustainable infrastructure solutions and making a positive impact on society.

