  ('Graduate Certificate of Arts', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Swinburne University of Technology Sarawak Campus' LIMIT 1), 'Diploma', 2490, '0.6 years', '["Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Graduate Certificate of Arts (TESOL) program at Swinburne University of Technology Sarawak Campus is specifically tailored to address the growing demand for a certificate course in Teaching English to Speakers of Other Languages (TESOL). This six-month program aims to facilitate the development of disciplinary knowledge in second language acquisition, with a specific focus on teaching English to non-native speakers. It equips both prospective and in-service teachers with essential basic tools for effective classroom practice in the field of TESOL. The program explores current theories and pedagogy in second/foreign language teaching, allowing students to gain a comprehensive understanding of the subject. By investigating classroom issues related to teaching TESOL and critically evaluating second/foreign language teaching methodologies, students develop a deeper insight into effective teaching practices. The Graduate Certificate of Arts (TESOL) program provides individuals with a solid foundation in TESOL and enhances their teaching capabilities in this specialized field.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

This unit will develop students’ knowledge of phonology of the English language to prepare them to teach English effectively. It will also develop students’ knowledge of the morphology and syntax of the English language, enabling students to compare and contrast English language grammar with that of one or more local major languages, and to apply this knowledge to teaching English grammar.

This unit will introduce students to the main approaches to the teaching of the English language, helping them to develop a critical understanding of the theoretical concepts underlying these approaches.

