  ('Master of Business Administration', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Swinburne University of Technology Sarawak Campus' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 12531, '2 years', '["Feb","May","Jul","Oct"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Business Administration (International) program at Swinburne University of Technology Sarawak Campus is a postgraduate qualification in general management that prepares students for careers in dynamic and uncertain work environments. This program equips students with the skills and knowledge necessary to thrive in unstructured work situations, navigate ill-defined workplaces, adapt to emerging technologies, and manage scarce natural resources. The course offers an integrated education in business management, catering to both pre-experience graduates with backgrounds in business or non-business academic disciplines, as well as post-experience graduates preparing for strategic leadership roles. By covering a broad range of business topics, the program provides students with a comprehensive understanding of management principles, strategic decision-making, organizational dynamics, and global business trends. Graduates of the program emerge with the capabilities to tackle complex challenges, seize opportunities, and assume leadership responsibilities in diverse professional settings. They are well-prepared to navigate the ever-changing business landscape and contribute to the success of organizations in a global context.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

To be eligible for the award of Master of Business Administration (International), students must complete 15 units of study (200 credit points) comprising of 14 units of study (12.5 credit points) and one (1) double unit of study (25 credit points).

