  ('Doctor of Philosophy', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Xiamen University Malaysia Campus' LIMIT 1), 'PhD', 2904, '3 years', '["Jan","May","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Chinese Studies program at Xiamen University boasts a rich history of academic excellence since its founding in 1921. Esteemed scholars such as Lu Xun and Lin Yutang were once part of its faculty. Recognized as the “National Talents Training and Research Base for Fundamental Studies in Humanities” and honored as a provider of “National Quality Courses” by China’s Ministry of Education, the program has emerged as a leader in Chinese linguistics and literature education.

The Doctor of Philosophy in Chinese Studies is designed to develop graduates who possess extensive knowledge of the field, essential academic skills for their careers, and the ability to conduct independent research that yields significant contributions to the discipline. This program meets the growing demand for professional education in the Chinese language and culture, addressing the need for highly skilled individuals in Malaysia and Southeast Asia''s job market.

