  ('Bachelor of Dentistry Degree', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'International Medical University (IMU)' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 31548, '5 years', '["Feb","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Dentistry degree is an extensive five-year undergraduate program designed to prepare students for a career in dentistry. It encompasses a broad spectrum of subjects, including dental anatomy, pathology, surgery, and restorative dentistry. Students acquire practical experience through clinical training and become eligible for licensure as dentists upon graduation.

Oral health is crucial in any society, leading to a consistently high demand for skilled dentists. Additionally, the ability to relieve pain and restore confidence in patients is incredibly rewarding. The Dentistry program at IMU offers two tracks to choose from, both of which provide dynamic and engaging learning environments. We employ a variety of innovative approaches, including interactive plenaries, team-based integrated learning (TBIL), workshops, student group dental practice, hospital placements, outreach programs, as well as virtual and augmented reality simulations. These methods, combined with supervised and independent on-demand simulations, ensure an integrated and personalized learning experience.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

