  ('Bachelor in Digital Health (Hons)', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'International Medical University (IMU)' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 7700, '3 years', '["Jul","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'Information and Communication Technologies (ICT) are driving a revolution in healthcare. The integration of ICT with health, healthcare, daily living, and society presents significant opportunities to enhance medical outcomes and improve efficiency. Rapidly evolving digital health tools, such as wearable devices, telehealth, telemedicine, and mobile health applications, have the potential to strengthen the relationship between physicians and patients. These tools accelerate the diagnostic process and enable the use of Artificial Intelligence (AI) to provide precise treatment recommendations. Such options empower patients to take a more active role in their health and promote preventive care by emphasizing nutrition, exercise, and wellness. Digital health tools also facilitate better management of chronic conditions outside traditional healthcare settings.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

