  ('Bachelor of Applied Science (Hons) in Medical Biotechnology', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'International Medical University (IMU)' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 9680, '3 years', '["Jul","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Applied Science (Hons) in Medical Biotechnology is an undergraduate program dedicated to the application of biotechnology principles within the medical field. It offers students a thorough understanding of the practical uses of biotechnology in healthcare and the pharmaceutical industry. Typically lasting three to four years, the program includes subjects such as biotechnology, molecular biology, genetics, biochemistry, immunology, pharmacology, and medical diagnostics. It emphasizes a balance between theoretical knowledge and practical skills.For centuries, Medical Biotechnology has played a crucial role in saving lives, from Edward Jenner’s development of the smallpox vaccine to the use of DNA technology for identifying SARS-CoV-2 and discovering a viable vaccine for COVID-19. This program offers a comprehensive curriculum that includes face-to-face classes, online lectures, hands-on laboratory experiences, workshops, seminars, and more, all aimed at preparing students to develop innovative products that enhance health and benefit humanity. Join us to acquire the knowledge that can make a difference and save lives.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

