  ('Bachelor of Nursing (Hons)', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'International Medical University (IMU)' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 5445, '4 years', '["Sep"]'::jsonb, 'Nursing is a specialized profession centered on caring, nurturing, educating, and conducting research within the healthcare system. Individuals who are eager to learn, possess leadership qualities, and have a strong commitment to enhancing the quality of life for the sick should consider studying Nursing. The nursing program at IMU aims to develop knowledgeable and skilled nurses who demonstrate critical thinking, compassion, motivation, and discipline.

For those qualified in this field, Nursing offers a wide array of career opportunities in education, clinical practice, research, and management. Nursing graduates can aspire to roles such as university professors, clinical specialists, research experts, or nursing directors. With experience, they may also establish their own nursing homes or nurseries, and there are numerous opportunities to pursue nursing careers internationally.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

