  ('Bachelor of Science (Hons) in Dietetics with Nutrition', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'International Medical University (IMU)' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 11000, '4 years', '["Jul","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Science (Hons) in Dietetics with Nutrition is an undergraduate program that combines the study of nutrition science and dietetics. Its goal is to provide students with a thorough understanding of how food and nutrition contribute to health promotion and disease prevention. The program typically spans three to four years and includes subjects such as biochemistry, physiology, food science, human nutrition, medical nutrition therapy, community nutrition, and research methods. It features a well-rounded curriculum that integrates theoretical knowledge with practical skills.In a world where eating habits significantly impact well-being, understanding the intricate connection between diet and health is essential. Dietitians play a crucial role in empowering individuals and communities to make food choices that promote good health. IMU’s Dietetic program will provide you with the knowledge and skills needed to assess the dietary needs of individuals and groups, offer consultations for disease management, and give professional guidance on developing healthier eating habits. Join us in creating healthier and brighter futures through the field of dietetics.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

