  ('Master in Health Professions Education', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'International Medical University (IMU)' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 10395, '2 years', '["Mar","Jul","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The IMU Postgraduate Programmes in Health Professions Education is a multi-exit program that includes three levels: Postgraduate Certificate, Postgraduate Diploma, and Master''s. These programs are specifically designed for health professionals engaged in or interested in education.

The curriculum is comprehensive, allowing students to gain a deep understanding of educational principles related to curriculum design, instructional methods, competency assessment, program evaluation, quality assessment, primary care education, clinical decision-making, health-related humanities, professionalism, ethics, and leadership skills in the field.

At the Master''s level, facilitators guide students as they advance toward becoming educational researchers or innovators.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

• Educating 21st Century Healthcare Professionals• Theories and Methods of Learning and Teaching in Health Professions Education• E-Learning in Health Professions Education• Work Based Learning in Health Professions Education• Assessment and Feedback• Laying the Foundation of Research• Curriculum Planning and Evaluation• Management and Leadership in Health Professions Education• Dissertation I• Dissertation II', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Healthcare educators/trainers \nCurriculum developers \nEducation consultants \nEducational researchers \nProgram directors/administrators \nProfessional development coordinators \nInstructional designers \nFaculty members/instructors"]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'A Bachelor’s Degree with a minimum CGPA of 2.50

