  ('Master in Pharmacy Practice', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'International Medical University (IMU)' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 11440, '1 year', '["Mar","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master in Pharmacy Practice is the first program of its kind offered at a Malaysian private university, featuring four areas of specialization with a research focus: Clinical Pharmacy, Social & Administrative Pharmacy, Pharmacy Management, and Clinical Research.

Students benefit from instruction and supervision by a distinguished faculty known for their excellence in various research activities, including published work in international peer-reviewed journals. They also have opportunities to collaborate with both local and international institutions on projects related to cancer, bioactive molecules, nutrition, and environmental health.

The program is available in both full-time and part-time formats, allowing pharmacists to continue their professional work while pursuing a flexible schedule that includes campus-based classes and experiential learning, supplemented by online support and access to tutors as needed.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

