  ('Master of Clinical Psychology', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'International Medical University (IMU)' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 17820, '2 years', '["Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Clinical Psychology is a graduate program that equips students with the skills necessary for the assessment, diagnosis, and treatment of mental health disorders. Graduates become clinical psychologists capable of working in various settings, providing evidence-based interventions, conducting assessments, and promoting mental health and well-being. The program includes practical skills training that enables graduates to apply evidence-based practices and theories effectively across diverse populations. As a result, they are well-prepared to take on roles in healthcare, education, research, corporate environments, and community settings. The program is provisionally accredited by the Malaysian Qualifications Agency (MQA), allowing graduates to apply for registration and practice clinical psychology with the Malaysian Allied Health Professions Council.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

