  ('Master of Counselling', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'International Medical University (IMU)' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 14850, '2 years', '["Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Counselling is a graduate program designed to train professionals in the counseling field, equipping them with the knowledge and skills needed to provide effective therapeutic support to individuals, couples, families, and groups. Graduates can pursue careers as licensed counselors in various settings, helping clients overcome challenges, promote mental health, and facilitate personal growth. The program includes practical skills training that meets both local and international standards, preparing graduates for leadership roles in counseling, teaching, research, and management. Accredited by the Malaysian Qualifications Agency (MQA), the program also complies with the standards set by the Malaysian Board of Counsellors. As a result, graduates are eligible to apply for registration with the Malaysian Board of Counsellors, enabling them to practice professionally in Malaysia..

