  ('Association of Chartered Certified Accountants (ACCA)(UOW)', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'University of Wollongong (UOW) Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 8036, '1 year', '["Jan","Mar","Jul","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Association of Chartered Certified Accountants (ACCA) at the University of Wollongong (UOW) is a prestigious program that prepares students for a successful career in accounting and finance. ACCA is the world’s leading professional accountancy body, boasting over 247,000 fully qualified members and 526,000 students globally. It focuses on developing innovative and strategic thinking accountants essential for navigating today’s fast-paced business environment.

The ACCA qualification comprises 13 exams divided into three levels: Applied Knowledge, Applied Skills, and Strategic Professional. Through this structured approach, students acquire comprehensive technical knowledge in accounting and finance, as well as insights into organizational management and strategies.

ACCA members typically work in various roles within the accounting and finance sectors, particularly in corporate environments. Pursuing an ACCA qualification equips you with the necessary skills and competencies, providing employers with confidence in your ability to excel in the field. This qualification is highly respected and offers numerous career opportunities for graduates.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

